<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva is a Brazilian trade unionist and founder of the Workers' Party who served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 2003 to 2010 and again from 2023. His first governments expanded social programmes such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsa-familia">Bolsa Família</a> and lifted millions out of poverty during a commodity boom. Convicted in the Car Wash investigation in 2017, he had the convictions annulled in 2021 and won the 2022 election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva.jpg" alt="Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo Stuckert/PR · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foto_oficial_de_Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva_(ombros)_denoise_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
